summary:
  A position that stands is noted in the log and the stream is left where it is.

history:
  Measured 2026-11-12 on Qt 6.12 with FFmpeg 9: a station that closed the
  connection, and one that held it and sent nothing, left the player saying
  it plays with the position at 29976 ms for as long as it was watched,
  170 s. The player's own error armed a heal that turned back because the
  player said it plays. The watch over the position is what hands such a
  stream on.

target:
  package/contents/ui/StandWatch.qml

find:
          app._streamDied();

replace:
          return false;

expect:
  Killed by test_invariants::test_a_stream_that_stands_is_handed_to_the_road_every_other_death_takes,
  which the gate runs first, and by tst_standwatch::test_a_position_that_stands_hands_the_stream_over_once.
  Line-neutral.
